WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Hong Kong's Hang Seng index for example was
down today after official data showed that

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:05.120
China's Exports dropped by more than 4% in
December, compared to the same period a year

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.120
earlier.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.939
It's the biggest drop in two years.

00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:12.290
China's global trade surplus also sank last
year, according to Chinese customs figures.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:18.270
But, crucially China's trade surplus with
the US jumped by more than 17% - prompting

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:22.780
fears that US president Donald Trump might
feel the need to crank upt the heat in the

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.470
simmering trade conflict between the world's
two biggest economies.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:31.099
China's weaker imports also worry analysts,
raising concerns the world economy might be

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:35.250
on track for a slowdown.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.360
Signs of an economic slowdown in China have
been hard to miss.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.940
And since the beginning of the year, the effects
are being felt elsewhere, too.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:49.620
In Britain last week , Jaguar LandRover said
it's cutting 4,500 jobs, due to a dramatic

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.530
drop off in sales in China.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.190
There was also a sharp sell off on global
equity markets

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.710
when Apple issued a profit warning due to
flagging Iphone sales in the world's second

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.860
largest economy.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:08.361
Shares in other companies heavily invested
in China also dropped after word got out that

00:01:08.361 --> 00:01:10.800
demand is softening.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.790
The global economy only now seems to be waking
up to the fact that growth is slowing fast

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:16.790
in China.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:24.230
GDP growth by some accounts will drop to just
over six percent by next year.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.180
China will remain a fast growing economy compared
to many other nations.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:33.460
But a slowdown now means a lot more than
it would have a couple of decades ago.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.810
That's because back then, China's surging
economy accounted for only a small part of

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.620
.. global economic performance.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:43.710
But today, it's nearly twenty percent.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:49.240
That means China's growth doesn't have to
cool too much, before things get really hot

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.320
in the countries who do business with it.

